From 7620b2f31a37bbd0389cc436599cbc753a54380e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 31 Dec 2025 18:24:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] Camera: Restore camera HALv1 support in AOSP 16 QPR2
 [1/2]

Originally ported by  Kyle Harrison <khwebmail@gmail.com>
on Thu Oct 28 13:54:35 2021 +0100

Revert "Camera: remove the camera device version check during statusCallback"
This reverts commit b8259798dc04226eb09114527cb124060fbf335b.

Adapted for AOSP 16 upstream's CameraCompatibilityInfo refactor: the
original patch predates the migration from a raw int rotationOverride
to android::content::res::CameraCompatibilityInfo across
CameraService/BasicClient/Client. CameraService::makeClient/
connectLegacy, api1/CameraClient, and
CameraProviderManager::DeviceInfo1::getCameraInfo were updated to use
CameraCompatibilityInfo instead of rotationOverride to match the
current Client/BasicClient constructor signatures and the
DeviceInfo::getCameraInfo virtual, which no longer compiles for the
HAL1 path without the fix.

Change-Id: I9e93ac967ff60eee9f3695a7cf2c6fc73e92a16c
